-- Frame Types
-- 1️⃣ Running Total
-- ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW
-- 2️⃣ Moving Window (Last 3 rows)
-- ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW
-- 3️⃣ Full Partition
-- ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING

-- Frame Clause — The Real Advanced Part

-- This is where 90% fail.

-- If you write:

-- SUM(salary) OVER (ORDER BY id)

-- Most databases default to:

-- RANGE BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW

-- Important difference:

-- ROWS

-- Counts physical rows.

-- RANGE

-- Counts values logically.

-- Example:

-- If two rows have same salary:

-- ROWS → treats them separately

-- RANGE → treats equal values as same frame boundary

-- In interviews → prefer ROWS to avoid confusion.
